# UI color palette usage

Use this palette site-wide:

- `--c-red`: arterial red
- `--c-green`: forest green
- `--c-blue`: royal blue
- `--c-cyan`: sky blue
- `--c-magenta`: burgundy
- `--c-yellow`: sun-burst yellow

Semantic usage guidance:

- **Posts and content surfaces**: prioritize blues (`--c-blue`, `--c-cyan`).
- **Call-to-actions**: prioritize yellows and reds (`--c-yellow`, `--c-red`).
- **Action-oriented elements** (where a user is being prompted to do something): prioritize green (`--c-green`).
- **Self-serving / promotional surfaces** (e.g. marketing cards, promo modules): prioritize burgundy (`--c-magenta`).

Card top-border guidance:

- Keep card top borders consolidated through shared card accent tokens/variables.
- Set card top-border color by card purpose:
  - action cards: green
  - primary acquisition card (`Join In`): arterial red (highest visual urgency)
  - promotional/marketing cards: burgundy
  - content/profile cards: blues

When updating UI styles, prefer changing shared tokens in `static/css/brand.css` rather than introducing new ad hoc accent colors.

Iconography (sizes 48 / 32 / 16, system-icon yellow hover, council-informed strokes): see `docs/ICONOGRAPHY.md` and `.cursor/rules/ui-iconography.mdc`.
